  "messages": [
    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "Choose one next planning step using the local decision below. Return exactly one listed statement and stop. No other planning choices have been supplied.\n{\"context\": \"Reception knows the visitor’s previous rooms and has a list of objects connected to those rooms.\", \"decision\": \"How should a returning visitor find something different?\", \"goal\": \"Help visitors find a satisfying route through the museum while keeping reception and volunteers manageable.\", \"problem\": \"A volunteer-run local museum wants to make a weekend visit easier to navigate. It has a modest collection, printed guides, a reception table, flexible volunteer positions, and several rooms that can remain open independently. The decisions concern interpretation and visitor organization, not conservation rules or safety policy.\"}\nCANDIDATE STATEMENTS:\nReception shows several connections from previous rooms and lets the visitor choose a new object. The visitor selects which link to follow.\nReception offers an unfamiliar object and explains its connection to a room the visitor saw before. A new destination is made approachable through a known connection.\nReception asks which previous room the visitor enjoyed and suggests a connected object elsewhere. A familiar interest provides a bridge to a new area."
    }
